# Fiat 126 two-door saloon, 1972-2000.
#
# The 126 replaced the 500: 3,129 mm long, 1,377 mm wide, 1,335 mm high,
# 1,840 mm wheelbase; 594-652 cc air-cooled twin, rear-mounted. Built in Italy to
# 1980 and in Poland as the 126p to 2000; a common cheap import in Britain.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiat_126
#
# Colours: White, Red, Blue and Green are documented Fiat colours of the period.
#
# Weight: 80 in total (white 25, red 25, blue 15, green 15).
#
# Speed 105 km/h; comfort 35/235 (line). Classes 0,1.
# Dates: 1972-2000 with a road tail to about 2008.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/fiat-126.blend. References:
# citycars/references/fiat-126/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
name=Fiat126(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=25
intro_year=1972
intro_month=10
retire_year=2008
retire_month=6
speed=105
class=0,1
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=35
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=235

